<h2 class="mt-14">Consent and purchaser suppression for Returns and reviews</h2>
<p>Classify required return and refund service, private feedback, public review invitations and promotional offers separately. Establish purpose and channel eligibility before enrollment and recheck current opt-outs, order, delivery, return and case state at dispatch. Exit matching-cart recovery after purchase; later eligible care or review requests need their own timing. An open case pauses related optional asks, while required service continues. Resolution alone does not restore marketing eligibility. Public review invitations should follow consistent experience-based rules rather than filtering for positive sentiment.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No documented consent</td><td>Hold optional marketing pending eligibility evidence; independently justified required service continues</td><td>A return request or purchase is not general marketing permission</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consented, never purchased</td><td>Only eligible optional education; no product review request before a credible experience</td><td>Early returns and reviews discounts train deal-waiting</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Check matching-cart recovery eligibility; no return or product review trigger from a cart alone</td><td>Returns And Reviews high-intent window deserves margin discipline</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Exit matching-cart recovery; schedule eligible care or review requests by delivery and experience</td><td>Post-checkout returns and reviews pitches trigger regret and opt-outs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>Pause related optional asks; recheck eligibility after resolution and continue required service</td><td>Open returns and reviews cases reset what the shopper tolerates</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Review clicks, purchases and preferences; opens alone do not prove inactivity</td><td>Returns And Reviews deliverability depends on pruning</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS consent present</td><td>Verify independent SMS permission, current opt-outs, and applicable timing and frequency rules</td><td>Returns And Reviews SMS complaints cost more per incident</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Use verified account purpose and terms; B2B status does not confer permission</td><td>Returns And Reviews retail promos can violate B2B terms</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>Validate addresses proportionately; free-domain use alone is not an abuse signal</td><td>Assess observed bounce, complaint and abuse signals</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Returns And Reviews QA profiles excluded from reporting</td><td>Returns And Reviews reporting stays clean without test noise</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>Document objective abuse controls; inferred occupation does not establish an exemption</td><td>Returns And Reviews consistency beats clever carve-outs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Legacy list without timestamps</td><td>Hold optional marketing while evidence is checked; repermission needs an independently eligible route</td><td>Missing timestamps require evidence review, not an automatic repermission send</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
